IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gdpr-core`

-- ============================================================================
-- gdpr-definitions.l4 -- ARTICLE 4 POINTS (1), (2), (6), (7), (8) OF REGULATION (EU) 2016/679.
-- Part of the keel, written by P1.  One function per defined term; the arguments are facts a
-- person could state.  Points (3)-(5), (9)-(26) are K2's; where a provision of P1 uses one of
-- them (consent, child, pseudonymisation, ...) it takes it as a plain input fact (PLAN.md section 4).
--
-- ANSWERS.  Every function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN.  JUST FALSE is given only where the definition
-- says "means" (the text's own no); each such branch carries a FALSE-kind comment and each
-- NOTHING branch a NOTHING-kind comment (assumed, not ruled: the rule of 2026-10-29).
-- Where an argument is documented as not changing the answer, the text says so in its own words
-- ("whether or not"); the argument is kept so the clause has a test.
-- ============================================================================

§ `Article 4(1): personal data, identifiable natural person, data subject`

-- src:39 | (1) ‘personal data’ means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person (‘data subject’); an identifiable natural person is one who can be identified, directly or indirectly, in particular by reference to an identifier such as a name, an identification number, location data, an online identifier or to one or more factors specific to the physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity of that natural person;
@ref Art 4(1) 'personal data': an identifiable natural person (src:39)
GIVEN `the ways the natural person can be identified` IS A LIST OF `Art 4(1) means of identification`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(1) the natural person is an identifiable natural person` MEANS
    IF NOT (null `the ways the natural person can be identified`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "means"): "means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person ... an identifiable natural person is one who can be identified, directly or indirectly"
    -- The list "in particular by reference to an identifier such as ..." is open; `some other means of identification` stands for any other way.

-- src:39 | (1) ‘personal data’ means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person (‘data subject’); an identifiable natural person is one who can be identified, directly or indirectly, in particular by reference to an identifier such as a name, an identification number, location data, an online identifier or to one or more factors specific to the physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity of that natural person;
@ref Art 4(1) 'personal data' (src:39)
GIVEN `the information relates to a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the natural person is identified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ways the natural person can be identified` IS A LIST OF `Art 4(1) means of identification`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(1) the information is personal data` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the information relates to a natural person`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person"
        IF `the natural person is identified`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE `Art 4(1) the natural person is an identifiable natural person` `the ways the natural person can be identified`
        -- an information about a natural person who is neither identified nor identifiable answers JUST FALSE from the line above (FALSE-kind: "means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person")

-- src:39 | (1) ‘personal data’ means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person (‘data subject’); an identifiable natural person is one who can be identified, directly or indirectly, in particular by reference to an identifier such as a name, an identification number, location data, an online identifier or to one or more factors specific to the physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity of that natural person;
@ref Art 4(1) ('data subject') (src:39)
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is identified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ways the person can be identified` IS A LIST OF `Art 4(1) means of identification`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(1) the person is a data subject` MEANS
    IF `the person is a natural person` AND `the information relates to the person`
    THEN `Art 4(1) the information is personal data` TRUE `the person is identified` `the ways the person can be identified`
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person ('data subject')": a person who is not a natural person, or to whom the information does not relate, is not the data subject

§ `Article 4(2): processing`

-- src:40 | (2) ‘processing’ means any operation or set of operations which is performed on personal data or on sets of personal data, whether or not by automated means, such as collection, recording, organisation, structuring, storage, adaptation or alteration, retrieval, consultation, use, disclosure by transmission, dissemination or otherwise making available, alignment or combination, restriction, erasure or destruction;
-- The OR in "performed on personal data or on sets of personal data" is two inputs under one inert chapeau, "the operations are performed": `on personal data` and `on sets of personal data`.
-- Each limb is named for its complement only, so that chapeau and limb read as the sentence; the chapeau is inert and does not change the answer.
-- Either limb alone is enough (OR).  It may be that a set of personal data is itself personal data, which would make the second limb redundant; Art 4(2) does not say, and this encoding leaves it to a lawyer (NOTES.md).
@ref Art 4(2) 'processing': performed on personal data or on sets of personal data (src:40)
GIVEN `the operations performed` IS A LIST OF `Art 4(2) operation on personal data`
      `on personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on sets of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the operations are performed by automated means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(2) the operations are processing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF null `the operations performed`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any operation or set of operations"
        IF NOT (    "the operations are performed" ...  `on personal data`
                                                    OR  `on sets of personal data`)
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words, "means"): "means any operation or set of operations which is performed on personal data or on sets of personal data": neither limb holds
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
        -- "whether or not by automated means": `the operations are performed by automated means` is not read, by the text's own words.
        -- "such as collection, ...": the named operations are examples; any other operation on personal data is also processing ("any operation").

§ `Article 4(6): filing system`

-- src:44 | (6) ‘filing system’ means any structured set of personal data which are accessible according to specific criteria, whether centralised, decentralised or dispersed on a functional or geographical basis;
@ref Art 4(6) 'filing system' (src:44)
GIVEN `the set is structured` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the set consists of personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the data are accessible according to specific criteria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `how the set is arranged` IS AN `Art 4(6) arrangement of a set of personal data`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(6) the set is a filing system` MEANS
    IF `the set is structured` AND `the set consists of personal data` AND `the data are accessible according to specific criteria`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means any structured set of personal data which are accessible according to specific criteria"
    -- "whether centralised, decentralised or dispersed on a functional or geographical basis": `how the set is arranged` is not read, by the text's own words.

§ `Article 4(7): controller`

-- src:45 | (7) ‘controller’ means the natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body which, alone or jointly with others, determines the purposes and means of the processing of personal data; where the purposes and means of such processing are determined by Union or Member State law, the controller or the specific criteria for its nomination may be provided for by Union or Member State law;
@ref Art 4(7) 'controller' (src:45)
GIVEN body IS A `Kind of person or body`
      `the body decides the purposes of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body decides the means of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Union or Member State law determines the purposes and means of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that law provides for the body as the controller, or sets criteria for nominating the controller that the body meets` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(7) the body is a controller` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF body EQUALS `not a person or body`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body"
        IF `the body decides the purposes of the processing` AND `the body decides the means of the processing`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `Union or Member State law determines the purposes and means of the processing`
           AND `that law provides for the body as the controller, or sets criteria for nominating the controller that the body meets`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means the natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body which, alone or jointly with others, determines the purposes and means of the processing of personal data; where the purposes and means of such processing are determined by Union or Member State law, the controller or the specific criteria for its nomination may be provided for by Union or Member State law"

-- src:45 | (7) ‘controller’ means the natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body which, alone or jointly with others, determines the purposes and means of the processing of personal data; where the purposes and means of such processing are determined by Union or Member State law, the controller or the specific criteria for its nomination may be provided for by Union or Member State law;
@ref Art 4(7) 'controller': alone or jointly with others (src:45)
GIVEN `the body decides the purposes of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body decides the means of the processing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body decides them jointly with another body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Art 4(7) how a controller determines the purposes and means`
`Art 4(7) how the body determines the purposes and means` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the body decides the purposes of the processing` AND `the body decides the means of the processing`)
        THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "alone or jointly with others" describes a body that "determines the purposes and means"; for a body that does not, or that is a controller only because Union or Member State law names it, the text does not say
        IF `the body decides them jointly with another body`
        THEN JUST `Art 4(7) jointly with others`
        OTHERWISE JUST `Art 4(7) alone`

§ `Article 4(8): processor`

-- src:46 | (8) ‘processor’ means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body which processes personal data on behalf of the controller;
@ref Art 4(8) 'processor' (src:46)
GIVEN body IS A `Kind of person or body`
      `the body processes personal data` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body processes it on behalf of the controller` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 4(8) the body is a processor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF body EQUALS `not a person or body`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body"
        IF `the body processes personal data` AND `the body processes it on behalf of the controller`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a natural or legal person, public authority, agency or other body which processes personal data on behalf of the controller"
